@context: The network — wait for a request to come back, and answer one with a file of your own.
@title: network

@var: {site} = http://localhost:8000

STEP 1: Wait for an API call
    NAVIGATE to {site}/quotes.html
    VERIFY that 'Simple things should be simple.' is present
    # WAIT FOR RESPONSE only sees responses that arrive after it starts, so it
    # goes right after the step that sets the request off.
    CLICK the 'Next quote' button
    WAIT FOR RESPONSE "api/quotes.json"
    VERIFY that 'Kent Beck' is present

STEP 2: MOCK — the page gets your data instead of the server's
    # A MOCK rule lasts for the rest of the session, across navigations.
    MOCK GET "api/quotes.json" with 'mocks/quotes.json'
    NAVIGATE to {site}/quotes.html
    VERIFY that 'Mocked wisdom, served from a file.' is present
    VERIFY that 'Alan Kay' is NOT present

DONE.
